<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate 21.70 pct in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate 21.70 pct in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate fell in this week's primary auction and demand rose, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	21.70	    -147	    21.70     21.70</p>
<p>91-Day	22.23	    - 63	    22.18     22.34</p>
<p>182-Day     22.73	    - 44	    22.65     22.75</p>
<p>350-Day     23.96				23.80     24.09</p>
<p>Last week the 357-day paper was assigned at 24.22 pct.  </p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	800 million pesos   2.50 bln pesos    3.12</p>
<p>91-Day	800 million pesos   5.02 bln pesos    6.28</p>
<p>182-Day     800 million pesos   5.29 bln pesos    6.61</p>
<p>350-Day     600 million pesos   2.26 bln pesos    3.77</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 5.02 on demand of 15.07 billion pesos compared with 4.05 the week before, on demand of 12.14 billion pesos the week before. Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			    0 basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			   11 basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			   2 basis points</p>
<p>    350-Day			  13 basis points</p>
<p>((--Dan Trotta, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9507))</p>
</text>
